WEBVTT

00:02.600 --> 00:05.430
Looks like there are some good ones around here.

00:05.440 --> 00:06.690
Yeah.

00:09.020 --> 00:15.650
Tsuwabuki-kun, you sure did something quite drastic.

00:15.970 --> 00:18.690
You two gave Yaeno-kun that mark,

00:21.130 --> 00:23.540
the mark of a friend who will protect the secret.

00:24.040 --> 00:27.590
That mark can be given to only one person, you know.

00:28.650 --> 00:30.690
If it happens again...

00:56.160 --> 01:02.870
Shining stars away bless

01:03.200 --> 01:08.080
chiisakutonaeru mahou no kotobawa

01:03.200 --> 01:08.080
Silently chanting the magical words

01:08.960 --> 01:10.710
『onegai。。。』

01:08.960 --> 01:10.710
"please"

01:11.000 --> 01:16.340
hoshizora samayou kaze ni notta maigo notsubu

01:11.000 --> 01:16.340
The lost grain riding the wind on the sky

01:16.340 --> 01:17.390
『kizuite。。。』

01:16.340 --> 01:17.390
Please notice

01:17.390 --> 01:25.270
tsutawara nakute porori ochita kono omoi

01:17.390 --> 01:25.270
Untold words, teardrops of feelings that fell down

01:25.770 --> 01:32.360
kagayaki dasuyo GARASU bin nonaka

01:25.770 --> 01:32.360
Show your shine inside the glass bottle

01:32.730 --> 01:39.740
manten no hoshi deatta KISEKI kimi ga soba ni itekureru nara

01:32.730 --> 01:39.740
If you will stay beside me perfect star of encountered miracles...

01:39.910 --> 01:47.120
Whatever the mystery, I will be able to gather my courage.

01:40.320 --> 01:47.120
donna fushigi mouke tomeru yuuki umare te yuku yo

01:47.460 --> 01:54.710
nanatsuiro ni hikaru houseki sora kara mai oriru

01:47.460 --> 01:54.710
Seven colored glittering gems flying down from the sky

01:54.710 --> 01:58.430
Scoop up the important fragments

01:55.130 --> 01:58.430
daijina KAKERA sukui agerune

01:58.430 --> 02:03.930
kowasa nuyou sotto。。。

01:58.430 --> 02:03.930
And secretly hold onto them tight

02:11.820 --> 02:14.600
Sumomo, how's this look?

02:14.600 --> 02:17.210
It looks really good, Nako-chan.

02:18.070 --> 02:20.020
Yep, just keep on going like that, you two.

02:20.890 --> 02:22.710
But compared to that...

02:28.400 --> 02:31.630
You must have never done this before, right Tsuwabuki-kun?

02:32.280 --> 02:33.530
Yeah...

02:33.940 --> 02:36.510
Akihime-san, please teach him how.

02:36.530 --> 02:37.490
Eh?!

02:37.490 --> 02:40.430
I think you can just show him the step-by-step method.

02:44.700 --> 02:45.660
Okay!

02:46.230 --> 02:47.840
You do this...

02:48.050 --> 02:49.960
then this.

02:50.540 --> 02:53.820
Then this... and then like this... and...

02:54.550 --> 02:56.520
And here! It's done!

02:57.250 --> 02:59.540
Ah, that looks good.

03:00.360 --> 03:02.480
This will be this year's main decoration.

03:02.480 --> 03:03.930
We'll name it the Wishing Star!

03:04.430 --> 03:06.060
Wishing Star?

03:06.060 --> 03:09.840
On July 7th, if you make a wish to this golden Wishing Star, your wish will definitely come true.

03:09.840 --> 03:12.320
It's decided. It'll be that.

03:12.860 --> 03:14.110
Okay!

03:15.590 --> 03:19.470
Golden Wishing Star

03:23.850 --> 03:25.140
The sun is setting...

03:29.400 --> 03:30.530
Alright...

03:35.000 --> 03:39.900
Is the star drop going to fall down today too?

03:40.330 --> 03:41.620
Yeah...

03:42.330 --> 03:45.180
You have a smile on your face...

03:45.300 --> 03:47.040
Eh? Yeah!

03:47.040 --> 03:48.660
I've been thinking...

03:48.670 --> 03:51.900
What should I wish for?

03:52.610 --> 03:56.970
Something like, "I wish to be a kinder person," or...

03:56.980 --> 03:59.540
"I wish to have more courage."

03:59.540 --> 04:04.660
Or even something like, "I wish to have bigger breasts."

04:04.800 --> 04:05.980
Just kidding.

04:08.490 --> 04:11.410
I hope tomorrow will be sunny.

04:11.640 --> 04:14.020
Since it will be Tanabata.

04:16.330 --> 04:17.420
It's shining!

04:17.420 --> 04:19.370
It's here, the star drop!

04:19.370 --> 04:20.560
Let's go, Yuki-chan!

04:24.440 --> 04:28.000
It went into the planetarium.

04:28.000 --> 04:31.490
Err, are we able to get inside that building?

04:36.860 --> 04:39.060
I don't see any opening.

04:39.250 --> 04:42.190
But we need to do something and get in.

04:43.330 --> 04:44.570
What is it?

04:51.290 --> 04:55.190
Umm... 'puro'... 'gu'...

04:55.560 --> 04:57.810
and also 'ridia'.

05:00.100 --> 05:02.350
Puro Guridia!

05:09.090 --> 05:10.830
T-This is...

05:12.460 --> 05:14.930
...a way in, right?

05:27.310 --> 05:28.580
Sumomo!

05:32.350 --> 05:35.380
It's so dark, Yuki-chan.

05:38.710 --> 05:42.190
The two drops before this were shining.

05:42.580 --> 05:44.730
Are you alright, Sumomo?

05:44.730 --> 05:46.420
How about we just give up for today?

05:46.420 --> 05:49.530
I'm alright since I'm with you, Yuki-chan.

05:49.530 --> 05:50.500
Maybe...

05:50.500 --> 05:52.710
Well, this is for Yuki-chan's sake after all.

05:52.920 --> 05:54.330
I'll do my best.

05:54.330 --> 05:55.530
Sumomo...

05:57.040 --> 05:58.730
Yuki-chan, look at that!

06:00.800 --> 06:02.580
The star drop!

06:05.160 --> 06:07.890
Alright, I'll try to catch it, Yuki-chan.

06:10.090 --> 06:12.190
Puruvu Ra-

06:25.650 --> 06:27.690
What kind of clothes are those?

06:27.950 --> 06:31.820
And you call yourself a Stellar Spinear?

06:37.170 --> 06:39.360
W-Who the hell are you?!

06:53.350 --> 06:56.160
Nice to meet you, Prima Plam.

06:57.530 --> 06:59.900
What? Prima...

06:59.900 --> 07:00.900
...Plam?

07:07.090 --> 07:11.700
I am the Saint Aspalas' Stellar Spinear, Prima Aspalas!

07:12.330 --> 07:16.000
Prima... Aspalas?

07:16.000 --> 07:17.200
Wow,

07:17.200 --> 07:18.750
that's so cool!

07:19.880 --> 07:21.200
Don't joke with me!

07:21.200 --> 07:23.560
We are enemies, you know?

07:23.570 --> 07:25.460
Rivals in gathering the star drops!

07:25.830 --> 07:27.800
She said enemy, do you know her?

07:27.800 --> 07:28.560
Nope.

07:29.780 --> 07:32.060
Is that doll your servant?

07:32.420 --> 07:34.050
Is it even competent?

07:38.530 --> 07:40.070
Di Pieroto.

07:40.830 --> 07:41.880
Huh?!

07:41.880 --> 07:43.140
Yuki-chan!

07:48.970 --> 07:50.690
What a strange little...

07:51.540 --> 07:52.740
Yuki-chan...!

07:53.570 --> 07:54.250
Sumomo!

07:54.400 --> 07:56.870
Give me back Yuki-chan!

08:00.050 --> 08:02.420
Are you alright, Yuki-chan?

08:02.420 --> 08:03.970
Y-Yeah.

08:03.960 --> 08:06.640
Hey, what was that for?

08:06.640 --> 08:08.580
Are you making fun of me?

08:09.860 --> 08:11.090
Umm...

08:11.100 --> 08:13.660
What you said about Prima...

08:13.670 --> 08:14.980
It's Prima Plam!

08:15.130 --> 08:15.880
Is that...

08:16.220 --> 08:17.640
really me?

08:18.250 --> 08:20.810
You have the Ladle and your servant...

08:20.810 --> 08:23.460
There is no way I'm wrong!

08:27.800 --> 08:30.760
Ruuche Ruvi Avis!

08:39.990 --> 08:42.540
Amazing!

08:48.710 --> 08:50.630
Puruvi Radius!

08:56.630 --> 08:58.080
Amazing...

08:58.420 --> 09:01.140
She captured the star drop!

09:01.880 --> 09:03.520
Congratulations...

09:03.520 --> 09:04.540
...Miss.

09:04.820 --> 09:06.650
This will be the third star drop.

09:07.330 --> 09:08.630
Third?

09:08.890 --> 09:10.370
The dog talked!

09:11.560 --> 09:13.220
You're able to do so too, right?

09:13.490 --> 09:15.450
And you're a doll on top of that.

09:15.670 --> 09:18.040
Arthur, bring that here.

09:19.660 --> 09:21.350
Here you are.

09:21.350 --> 09:23.120
No, not the lunch box!

09:23.390 --> 09:24.880
I am really sorry.

09:25.460 --> 09:26.760
Here it is.

09:26.830 --> 09:29.600
What do I need a mop for? No!

09:30.210 --> 09:31.590
Well then, this one.

09:31.590 --> 09:33.710
No, that's wrong! Wrong!

09:33.690 --> 09:35.030
Sorry, sorry!

09:33.710 --> 09:37.740
What are you doing?! I mean that, that thing! Don't you know?

09:35.740 --> 09:36.880
Umm...

09:37.740 --> 09:39.140
I'm really sorry! How about this?

09:37.740 --> 09:39.140
These two...

09:39.610 --> 09:41.280
That's right, it's this one.

09:42.210 --> 09:44.390
Bring that to her.

09:47.630 --> 09:51.510
This book looks similar to Yuki-chan's book.

09:51.510 --> 09:54.260
Open the pages please.

09:55.820 --> 09:59.090
Don't tell me your magical power is only that much?

09:59.090 --> 10:01.340
You don't have to be so mean!

10:01.340 --> 10:03.770
Being mean? You must be kidding!

10:03.770 --> 10:05.840
Listen, this is a fight, you know.

10:06.720 --> 10:07.830
A fight?

10:08.030 --> 10:11.850
That's right. I want a fair fight in gathering the star drops...

10:11.850 --> 10:15.140
with someone whose power corresponds to mine.

10:15.140 --> 10:19.330
But since you can't even open my Recipe,

10:19.330 --> 10:22.910
that means your level is much lower compared to mine.

10:23.170 --> 10:26.880
You... Are you really the Prima Plam?

10:27.480 --> 10:28.890
Umm...

10:30.710 --> 10:32.650
Even if you don't know about it...

10:32.650 --> 10:35.060
...you are still destined to fight with me.

10:35.210 --> 10:36.920
Improve on your skills.

10:37.810 --> 10:40.330
If you want to gather the star drops, that is.

10:40.340 --> 10:44.770
You won't be getting any of the star drops from me!

10:46.380 --> 10:47.120
Sumomo...

10:48.590 --> 10:49.920
Wait!

11:07.730 --> 11:09.320
Sumomo?

11:09.320 --> 11:10.600
What happened?

11:12.280 --> 11:17.030
If you feel sick, how about letting me handle giving out the bamboo decorations at the park?

11:17.030 --> 11:19.740
I-I'm alright, Nako-chan.

11:19.740 --> 11:21.330
Look, I'm healthy.

11:21.640 --> 11:23.700
I'm alright, really.

11:23.700 --> 11:26.460
I can hand out the bamboo decorations.

11:27.230 --> 11:28.530
Sumomo...

11:30.720 --> 11:32.060
<i>Akihime...</i>

11:37.670 --> 11:39.170
Sumomo...

11:39.170 --> 11:41.100
Cheer up.

11:41.100 --> 11:44.180
I'm sorry, Yuki-chan.

11:44.180 --> 11:48.130
I wasn't able to catch the star drop...

11:48.130 --> 11:50.930
Don't worry, there is always next time.

11:51.930 --> 11:53.330
But...

11:54.800 --> 11:55.870
Sorry...

12:00.980 --> 12:02.300
<i>Akihime...</i>

12:04.120 --> 12:07.040
<i>In any case, we have to stop that other girl. </i>

12:07.790 --> 12:09.320
I see...

12:09.320 --> 12:12.080
Another Stellar Spinear appeared.

12:12.080 --> 12:14.800
Stop deploring and explain about it.

12:16.610 --> 12:20.350
But this doesn't always mean it's bad news. Maybe...

12:20.350 --> 12:21.300
Maybe...?

12:22.240 --> 12:25.760
For now, I can only say 'maybe'.

12:25.780 --> 12:27.730
What's with that answer?

12:28.450 --> 12:32.540
It's not fair for Akihime.

12:32.540 --> 12:34.850
Even last night she was...

12:36.440 --> 12:40.090
I see. So Akihime-san did...

12:41.070 --> 12:43.000
W-What?

12:43.110 --> 12:44.570
Nothing at all.

12:44.570 --> 12:48.270
Anyway, we have to go to the park today, right?

12:52.660 --> 12:54.140
Here you go.

12:55.300 --> 12:57.040
Thank you, Onee-chan.

12:57.390 --> 13:00.700
This decoration here is called the Wishing Star.

13:00.700 --> 13:01.930
Wishing Star?

13:02.130 --> 13:05.170
That's right. If you make a wish to this star,

13:05.170 --> 13:06.960
your wish will definitely come true.

13:07.910 --> 13:08.770
Thank you!

13:13.930 --> 13:17.800
Well then, I'm going to help walk these kids home.

13:17.940 --> 13:19.790
Thank you, Onee-chan!

13:19.790 --> 13:21.020
Bye bye.

13:21.730 --> 13:24.320
I hope your wish comes true.

13:24.320 --> 13:25.530
Bye bye.

13:40.600 --> 13:42.090
Akihime...

13:51.800 --> 13:53.920
I have to cheer up!

14:00.650 --> 14:05.650
From now on I will keep doing my best for Yuki-chan's sake.

14:05.880 --> 14:07.740
For Yuki-chan's sake!

14:24.600 --> 14:25.670
Akihime.

14:27.010 --> 14:28.220
Tsuwabuki-kun.

14:28.540 --> 14:31.000
Looks like you guys are done.

14:31.000 --> 14:34.490
I hurried here from Kisaragi-sensei's room.

14:36.100 --> 14:39.110
Umm, did you hear everything?

14:39.110 --> 14:40.740
Yeah.

14:40.740 --> 14:42.010
Sorry.

14:44.830 --> 14:46.090
Umm...

14:47.450 --> 14:50.980
A-Are you alright?

14:51.770 --> 14:57.260
Because today, Akihime was different than usual.

14:59.180 --> 15:00.820
Umm...

15:01.660 --> 15:03.650
T-Thank you.

15:04.910 --> 15:09.120
Umm I... I was just feeling kind of down.

15:09.120 --> 15:12.080
A lot of things happened.

15:13.240 --> 15:14.760
I see.

15:17.460 --> 15:21.680
But tonight will be Tanabata, so...

15:21.680 --> 15:27.960
When I think about the people who will make their wishes to the Wishing Star,

15:28.830 --> 15:31.480
I feel better.

15:32.160 --> 15:33.490
Is that strange?

15:33.900 --> 15:35.190
No.

15:43.550 --> 15:45.970
That's right, we need to clean up.

15:50.220 --> 15:51.710
You know what?

15:52.110 --> 15:54.370
Maybe I'm being nosy, but...

15:58.370 --> 16:03.060
Doing something for someone else's sake or something like that...

16:03.380 --> 16:07.580
You shouldn't have to worry about those things so much.

16:07.580 --> 16:10.050
Because doing that will make you suffer, Akihime.

16:11.110 --> 16:12.430
Right?

16:13.020 --> 16:15.000
Even for that person called Yuki-chan...

16:15.000 --> 16:17.520
...he wouldn't be happy seeing you suffer.

16:26.320 --> 16:27.780
What should I do?

16:28.620 --> 16:32.090
What should I do so Yuki-chan will be happy?

16:33.270 --> 16:36.560
I can't say it any better, but...

16:38.690 --> 16:42.520
Just be yourself. I think that is enough.

16:42.520 --> 16:43.670
Maybe...

16:56.910 --> 16:58.240
Sumomo-chan, welcome back.

16:58.780 --> 17:00.930
I'm home, Dad.

17:00.940 --> 17:02.510
Perfect timing.

17:02.510 --> 17:05.300
I forgot something important at work.

17:05.300 --> 17:07.440
So can I leave you to watch the house?

17:07.540 --> 17:08.670
No problem.

17:08.670 --> 17:09.180
Thanks.

17:09.640 --> 17:13.740
I'll come home as soon as I can, but I'll call if I'm going to be late.

17:13.750 --> 17:15.020
Okay.

17:15.020 --> 17:18.770
Oh yeah, I prepared dinner, but...

17:18.770 --> 17:23.990
if it's a problem, you can eat leftover curry in the refrigerator.

17:23.990 --> 17:25.470
Got it!

17:25.470 --> 17:26.740
Well then, please.

17:27.020 --> 17:28.810
See ya later!

17:30.420 --> 17:32.750
Watching the house, huh?

17:33.790 --> 17:35.420
Alright!

17:35.530 --> 17:37.560
Good for you, Sumomo.

17:37.560 --> 17:39.820
We can somehow see the Milky Way.

17:42.240 --> 17:47.240
The kids who got the bamboo decorations must be happy too.

17:47.340 --> 17:48.830
That's right.

17:50.010 --> 17:51.390
Sumomo?

17:51.390 --> 17:53.110
Hey, Yuki-chan.

17:54.200 --> 17:56.980
Umm, actually I...

17:56.980 --> 17:59.700
was thinking a lot today.

18:01.860 --> 18:07.370
From now on, that girl from yesterday will probably...

18:07.910 --> 18:09.910
...take all of the star drops.

18:09.910 --> 18:11.170
I don't know...

18:12.400 --> 18:15.210
I probably won't be...

18:15.530 --> 18:18.920
any use to Yuki-chan anymore.

18:18.920 --> 18:21.670
That's what I thought about.

18:22.160 --> 18:23.470
That's not true!

18:23.470 --> 18:24.710
That's why...

18:26.240 --> 18:29.530
I searched for what I could do.

18:29.530 --> 18:36.210
Something that even <i>I </i>can do, for Yuki-chan's sake.

18:38.000 --> 18:40.680
I will always be there with a smile...

18:41.350 --> 18:46.560
Because that is the only thing I can do.

18:46.560 --> 18:47.240
Look!

18:57.380 --> 18:58.420
Eh...?

19:03.040 --> 19:05.370
I'm... sorry...

19:06.360 --> 19:10.160
I... can't seem to smile...

19:11.850 --> 19:13.920
Sumomo...

19:15.510 --> 19:16.680
Please...

19:17.270 --> 19:23.350
Star-sama, please let me smile.

19:29.640 --> 19:31.070
Sumomo...

19:35.890 --> 19:38.300
Sumomo, Sumomo!

19:38.610 --> 19:41.500
Open your eyes, slowly.

19:51.720 --> 19:53.930
Yuki-chan, this is...?

19:54.040 --> 19:57.420
Sumomo, your wishes will come true!

20:01.160 --> 20:02.230
Yuki-chan!

20:02.590 --> 20:04.090
Yuki-chan, Yuki-chan!

20:04.090 --> 20:06.350
Thank you, Yuki-chan!

20:07.160 --> 20:08.470
Yuki-chan.

20:10.780 --> 20:12.120
That's right.

20:12.120 --> 20:15.800
I was thinking of a present for you.

20:16.530 --> 20:18.300
A present?

20:18.520 --> 20:23.750
Last night the spell by Aspalas-san was really beautiful, so...

20:23.750 --> 20:27.760
I thought I could see it again with Yuki-chan.

20:27.760 --> 20:28.830
That's why...

20:29.350 --> 20:30.720
I'll try my best.

20:36.900 --> 20:41.670
Please, golden Wishing Star...

20:41.670 --> 20:44.200
I want to show this to Yuki-chan!

20:48.460 --> 20:50.770
Ruuche Ruvi Avis!

21:06.320 --> 21:08.160
I did it!

21:10.170 --> 21:11.960
You did it, Sumomo!

21:11.960 --> 21:13.300
Yuki-chan!

21:13.300 --> 21:15.000
That's amazing, Sumomo!

21:15.000 --> 21:17.210
Thanks to you, Yuki-chan.

21:17.210 --> 21:18.470
Thank you,

21:18.470 --> 21:20.130
Yuki-chan.

21:20.970 --> 21:22.170
Thank you...

21:23.480 --> 21:24.780
...Tsuwabuki-kun.

21:27.470 --> 21:30.250
This can't be...

21:31.120 --> 21:32.860
What did you say?!

21:32.860 --> 21:37.100
She mastered the "Sakuya Shirimoshinakata" skill in one night?

21:37.100 --> 21:38.690
Yes, Miss.

21:38.690 --> 21:43.530
It looked so beautiful, I couldn't help but stare at it.

21:43.530 --> 21:45.710
I never asked your opinion!

21:45.710 --> 21:47.250
Y-Yes!

21:47.250 --> 21:48.760
Please forgive me!

21:50.920 --> 21:53.080
Just as I thought, that girl is...

21:56.880 --> 21:59.670
<i>The day after the unforgettable Tanabata evening...</i>

22:00.200 --> 22:01.570
Alright everyone.

22:01.570 --> 22:03.470
Be quiet please.

22:03.470 --> 22:08.010
Just for today I will be your homeroom teacher.

22:08.460 --> 22:13.860
First off, an introduction of a new transfer student.

22:15.040 --> 22:17.180
<i>Transferring at this time?</i>

22:24.430 --> 22:26.650
A beautiful girl with glasses!

22:26.890 --> 22:28.430
A very high grade!

22:28.430 --> 22:30.120
Hey boys! Don't stand up!

22:32.010 --> 22:33.340
I'm Yuuki Nona.

22:35.730 --> 22:39.090
<i>That was the dawn of the troubles ahead.</i>

22:51.540 --> 22:55.090
kira kira no hoshikuzu ha maru de

22:51.540 --> 22:55.090
Fragments of glittering stars

22:55.090 --> 22:58.380
koi suru otome no kiseki

22:55.090 --> 22:58.380
are just like the miracles of a girl in love

22:58.630 --> 23:02.180
kinou mada no watashi ha doko he

22:58.630 --> 23:02.180
Where did the cleverness from yesterday go,

23:02.180 --> 23:05.100
nanika chigau RABIRINSU

23:02.180 --> 23:05.100
Since it's like a labyrinth now

23:05.600 --> 23:09.350
dan dan wakan naku naru

23:05.600 --> 23:09.350
Slowly becoming confused

23:09.520 --> 23:12.360
（doushi you　doushi you）

23:09.520 --> 23:12.360
What do I do? What do I do?

23:12.610 --> 23:19.570
don don afurete kuru　AH　HAHAHA

23:12.610 --> 23:19.570
